    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. It sounds like the enforcement side is mostly focused on things like \"sovereignty\" and \"deterrence,\" which feel a bit more abstract or even ideological compared to the very concrete economic benefits of the pathways approach you mentioned earlier. \n\nWhen the committee asks for a final recommendation on which model actually scales better for the country's future, is there any way to argue that the enforcement approach is actually more economically sound, or is that argument fundamentally weaker?",
