      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Arguing for the economic soundness of the enforcement model is challenging because its primary economic benefit is largely defensive, focused on *preventing* negative externalities. A stronger economic argument would pivot on signaling strong control to global markets, potentially boosting investor confidence in stability. However, critics would counter that this constriction limits the benefits of diverse labor pools crucial for modern economic dynamism, making the growth potential inherently weaker than the integration model.",
